      "content": "These new federal environmental regulations are a massive hit to small-scale manufacturing because they impose disproportionate compliance costs that only large corporations can absorb. Small shops often lack the capital to upgrade equipment or hire specialized staff, forcing them to either shut down or sell out to big players who can easily meet these standards. This regulatory overreach effectively acts as a tax on local entrepreneurship, stifling innovation and driving economic growth out of our communities.",
      "source": "target",
